# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Grid Master — optional mail configuration
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing here is required: out of the box the website delivers bookings through
# the free FormSubmit relay (activate the recipient inbox once — see README).
#
# Set the variables below to send booking e-mails from your own domain instead.
# They are server-side only (Netlify / Vercel environment variables), so the API
# key is never exposed to visitors.
#
#   MAIL_PROVIDER=resend            # resend | sendgrid | brevo | webhook
#   MAIL_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxx    # API key of that provider
#   MAIL_FROM="Grid Master Bookings <bookings@yourdomain.com>"
#   MAIL_TO=contactgridmaster@gmail.com     # optional (this is the default)
#   MAIL_CC=engineer@yourdomain.com,office@yourdomain.com   # optional
#
# Provider "webhook" needs no account at all: point it at a Google Apps Script
# web app (see docs/google-apps-script-mail-relay.gs) or any Zapier/Make hook.
#   MAIL_PROVIDER=webhook
#   MAIL_WEBHOOK_URL=https://script.google.com/macros/s/xxxx/exec
#   MAIL_WEBHOOK_SECRET=any-long-random-text    # optional
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build-time options (Vite). Copy the ones you need into a `.env` file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_MAIL_ENDPOINT=/api/send-booking   # where the browser posts bookings
# VITE_MAIL_BACKEND=on                   # set to "off" to skip the server relay
# VITE_MAIL_WEBHOOK_URL=                 # personal relay (Google Apps Script URL)
# VITE_MAIL_WEBHOOK_SECRET=              # optional shared secret for that relay
# VITE_WEB3FORMS_KEY=                    # optional extra relay access key
#
# No build step needed for the personal relay either: paste the URL straight
# into the website's Mail Delivery Center page (/mail-delivery).
